<odoo>
    <record id="kt_dataset_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="model">kt.dataset</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form>
                <header>
                    <field
                        name="state"
                        widget="statusbar"
                        statusbar_visible="draft,validated"
                    />
                </header>
                <sheet>
                    <group name="main">
                        <group name="left">
                            <field name="model_id" />
                            <field name="name" />
                        </group>
                        <group name="right">
                            <field name="group_ids" widget="many2many_tags" />
                            <field
                                name="company_id"
                                groups="base.group_multi_company"
                            />
                        </group>
                    </group>
                    <group colspan="1">
                        <field name="line_ids" nolabel="1">
                            <kanban>
                                <templates>
                                    <t t-name="card">
                                        <field name="name" />
                                        <field name="kind" />
                                        <field name="active" optional="hide" />
                                        <field
                                            name="group_ids"
                                            widget="many2many_tags"
                                        />
                                    </t>
                                </templates>
                            </kanban>
                        </field>
                    </group>
                </sheet>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="kt_dataset_line_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="model">kt.dataset.line</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form>
                <group>
                    <group colspan="2">
                        <field
                            name="definition"
                            widget="ace"
                            options="{'mode': 'python'}"
                        />
                        <field
                            name="validation_msg"
                            string="Validation"
                            readonly="1"
                            colspan="2"
                            decoration-danger="validation_msg"
                            invisible="not validation_msg"
                            placeholder="Definition validated"
                        />
                    </group>
                </group>
                <div class="mb-3" invisible="kind != 'data'">
                    <details>
                        <summary class="fw-bold">Polars syntax of a "Data" tile</summary>
                        <div class="p-2">
                            <p>The definition is a Python snippet that transforms the rows of the dataset with
                                <a
                                    href="https://docs.pola.rs/api/python/stable/reference/"
                                    target="_blank"
                                >polars</a>. It runs in a restricted sandbox : only what is listed here.</p>
                            <h6>Skeleton</h6>
                            <p>The first line names the variables, <code>output = input</code>, then each line
                                transforms the output. The output must be a table.</p>
                            <pre>d_next = d
d_next = d_next.filter(pl.col("state") == "sale")
d_next = d_next.group_by("user_id").agg(pl.col("amount_untaxed").sum().alias("Revenue"))
d_next = d_next.sort("Revenue", descending=True).head(10)</pre>
                            <h6>What the snippet has</h6>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>d</code> : the rows of the dataset the user may read, already filtered by the
                                    panel period and dimensions (a polars LazyFrame).</li>
                                <li><code>pl</code> : polars.</li>
                                <li><code>odoo_url</code> : the base url of Odoo, to build links.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <h6>Columns</h6>
                            <ul>
                                <li>The stored fields of the model. A many2one gives its <b>name</b> in
                                    <code>partner_id</code> and its <b>id</b> in <code>partner_id_</code>.</li>
                                <li>Relational paths declared for the dataset :
                                    <code>pl.col("partner_id.country_id.name")</code>.</li>
                                <li>Date parts : <code>pl.col("date_order.year")</code>, and <code>.quarter</code>,
                                    <code>.month</code>, <code>.week</code>, <code>.day</code>.</li>
                                <li>The names given with <code>.alias()</code> are the column titles of the table.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <h6>Allowed</h6>
                            <ul>
                                <li><b>Functions</b> : <code>pl.col</code>, <code>lit</code>, <code>when</code>,
                                    <code>sum</code>, <code>mean</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>min</code>,
                                    <code>max</code>, <code>first</code>, <code>last</code>, <code>len</code>,
                                    <code>all</code>, <code>any</code>, <code>int_range</code>,
                                    <code>date_range</code>, <code>struct</code>, <code>list</code>,
                                    <code>concat</code>, <code>concat_str</code>, <code>sum_horizontal</code>,
                                    <code>mean_horizontal</code>, <code>select</code>, and the types
                                    <code>String</code>, <code>Int64</code>, <code>Int32</code>,
                                    <code>Float64</code>, <code>Float32</code>, <code>Boolean</code>,
                                    <code>Date</code>, <code>Datetime</code>, <code>Decimal</code>...</li>
                                <li><b>On the table</b> : <code>filter</code>, <code>with_columns</code>,
                                    <code>select</code>, <code>group_by</code>, <code>agg</code>,
                                    <code>sort</code>, <code>rename</code>, <code>cast</code>, <code>join</code>,
                                    <code>unique</code>, <code>pivot</code>, <code>limit</code>, <code>head</code>,
                                    <code>tail</code>, <code>slice</code>, <code>drop</code>,
                                    <code>drop_nulls</code>, <code>fill_null</code>, <code>explode</code>,
                                    <code>unnest</code>, <code>sample</code>, <code>with_row_index</code>,
                                    <code>sql</code>...</li>
                                <li><b>On an expression</b> : aggregations (<code>sum</code>, <code>mean</code>,
                                    <code>median</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>n_unique</code>, <code>std</code>...),
                                    conditions (<code>when</code>/<code>then</code>/<code>otherwise</code>,
                                    <code>is_in</code>, <code>is_null</code>, <code>is_between</code>), text
                                    (<code>contains</code>, <code>starts_with</code>, <code>replace</code>,
                                    <code>strip_chars</code>, <code>to_lowercase</code>...), dates
                                    (<code>year</code>, <code>month</code>, <code>truncate</code>,
                                    <code>offset_by</code>, <code>to_date</code>...), maths (<code>round</code>,
                                    <code>abs</code>, <code>ceil</code>, <code>floor</code>, <code>sqrt</code>...),
                                    windows (<code>over</code>, <code>rank</code>, <code>cum_sum</code>,
                                    <code>shift</code>, <code>diff</code>...), <code>alias</code>,
                                    <code>cast</code>, <code>fill_null</code>.</li>
                                <li><b>Python</b> : <code>abs all any bool dict enumerate float int isinstance len
                                    list max min pow range round set sorted str sum tuple zip</code>.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <h6>Forbidden</h6>
                            <p><code>import</code>, <code>lambda</code>, <code>def</code>, <code>class</code>,
                                loops (<code>for</code>, <code>while</code>), <code>try</code>, <code>with</code>,
                                <code>del</code>, any name starting with <code>_</code>, calls that are not in
                                the lists above (<code>open</code>, <code>eval</code>, <code>getattr</code>...) and
                                the methods that run Python code on each row (<code>map_elements</code>,
                                <code>apply</code>, <code>map_batches</code>...). An error is shown in the tile.</p>
                            <h6>Good to know</h6>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Only the first 500 rows are shown (<code>TILE_MAX_ROWS</code>) : sort and
                                    <code>head</code> in the snippet.</li>
                                <li>Numbers are formatted by the tile (thousands, decimals) : do not cast them to text.</li>
                                <li>A cell written <code>[label](url)</code> is drawn as a link, if the url is an Odoo
                                    one :
                                    <pre>pl.concat_str([pl.lit("["), pl.col("partner_id"), pl.lit("]("), pl.lit(odoo_url),
    pl.lit("/odoo/sale.order/"), pl.col("id").cast(pl.String), pl.lit(")")]).alias("Customer")</pre>
                                </li>
                                <li>A method that needs the rows in memory (<code>pivot</code>, <code>transpose</code>,
                                    <code>describe</code>...) is supported : the snippet is run again on the filtered
                                    rows.</li>
                                <li>A conditional column :
                                    <pre>pl.when(pl.col("amount_untaxed") &gt; 1000).then(pl.lit("big")).otherwise(pl.lit("small")).alias("Size")</pre>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>
                <group>
                    <group>
                        <group>
                            <field name="kind" widget="radio" />
                            <field
                                name="group_ids"
                                widget="many2many_tags"
                            />
                            <field name="user_id" />
                        </group>
                        <group>
                            <field name="name" />
                            <field name="panel_id" />
                            <field name="col_span" />
                            <field name="tile_height" />
                            <field
                                name="active"
                                widget="boolean_toggle"
                            />
                        </group>
                    </group>
                </group>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="kt_dataset_kanban" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="model">kt.dataset</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <kanban>
                <templates>
                    <t t-name="card">
                        <h4>
                            <field name="model_id" />
                        </h4>
                        <field name="name" />
                        <field name="sequence" widget="handle" />
                    </t>
                </templates>
            </kanban>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="kt_dataset_search" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="model">kt.dataset</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <search>
                <filter name="name" />
            </search>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="kt_dataset_action" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Datasets</field>
        <field name="res_model">kt.dataset</field>
        <field name="view_mode">kanban,form</field>
    </record>

    <menuitem
        id="kpiten_menu"
        parent="kpiten_app"
        sequence="10"
        action="kt_dataset_action"
    />
</odoo>
